provenance.prompt:
EDIT/REDRAW the first reference as a clean-roomier transparent pixel-art sprite sheet of the SAME Juniper Vale 360-degree tomahawk dunk. Use the other two references only to keep her canon face, hair, uniform and pixel style. Preserve the same 15-action order and body proportions, but create a spacious exact 5-column by 3-row sheet at 1800x1200 so no body approaches a cell or canvas edge. One complete unique pose per cell in row-major order. Keep each pose at least 32px from the outer image edge and at least 24px of clear transparent gutter between neighboring pose silhouettes; pose2's hair must have at least 40px top clearance. Uniformly reduce figures as needed to honor margins. Every hand, shoe, ponytail and limb remains fully inside its own cell. No overlaps, no cropped/cut-off anatomy, no stray detached pixels.

Juniper canon: compact natural human woman, warm light skin, focused dark eyes, abundant dark-purple curls in a high ponytail with a small gold tie, blank Chicago Condas purple-and-gold jersey and shorts with NO numbers, text, logo or marks, dark knee pads, white socks, purple-and-gold basketball shoes. Keep her identical across all views and match existing 16-bit arcade pixel art.

Action sequence is EXACTLY:
0 right-facing approach with invisible ball cradled in right hand beside hip, left hand near chest;
1 plant lead foot, sink hips, pull right elbow sharply back, open left palm;
2 takeoff, feet leave floor, right hand rises beside face with bent elbow;
3 early ascent, knee lifts, right hand passes behind crown;
4 mid-ascent, knees gather and right hand drops behind crown into a deep backswing;
5 secure the invisible ball behind crown in the right hand, elbow maximally flexed;
6 late ascent, upper arm vertical, forearm cocked backward like a hammer;
7 peak with forearm still folded behind head;
8 start descent, right shoulder drives forward and elbow forcefully begins extension;
9 straighten right arm overhead into the steep downward chop;
10 one direct release through an imaginary rim plane, right wrist folds down and fingers open;
11 steep downward right-arm follow-through, left arm braces outward;
12 drop away, empty right elbow folds beside torso and shoulders recover;
13 landing approach with legs unfolding and arms open, right hand lower than left;
14 land on both feet, knees absorb impact, right fist relaxed by thigh and left hand outside hip.

No basketball is painted in the sheet; the ball is separate runtime art. Do not draw a rim, background, court, shadow, captions, grid lines or props. Keep all fifteen silhouettes distinct, complete, separated, generously padded and easy to crop.

